# THE GAZE UP AT THE RING (19_orbit `gaze`, 41_shoulder): over the shoulder at
# dusk, a pass standing high on the bearing the view faces. Level, the wheel is
# above the frame; the mouse tips the view up past the ordinary limit because
# the ring holds the gaze, and the whole wheel, gold over a dark land, comes
# into the frame. Turned away, the view eases home.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/orbit_gaze.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=21.5 --orbit=zenith@23.5/225 --view=shoulder --weather=clear:0
wait 2
await ring_up 5
shot 00-level
mouse 0,-2400 1.5
wait 0.5
await ring 5
shot 01-looking-up-at-it
wait 2
shot 02-still-looking
mouse -900,0 1
wait 1.5
shot 03-turned-away
